/*
Detection Rule: AWS Root Account Console or API Usage
Author: Bryan Jorge
MITRE ATT&CK: T1078.004 - Valid Accounts: Cloud Accounts
Severity: Critical
Description: Detects any use of the AWS root account via console login or
programmatic API calls. Root account usage should be near-zero in a
well-managed AWS environment. Any activity — even a single event — warrants
immediate investigation. AWS best practice mandates root is used only for
initial setup and specific billing tasks that cannot be delegated.
*/

index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
    userIdentity.type="Root"

| eval event_type=case(
    eventName="ConsoleLogin",                      "Console Login",
    eventSource="signin.amazonaws.com",            "Sign-In Event",
    1==1,                                          "API Call")

| eval mfa_used=coalesce(additionalEventData.MFAUsed, "No")

/* Score based on action sensitivity and MFA posture */
| eval risk_score=0
| eval risk_score=if(event_type="Console Login" AND mfa_used="No",  risk_score+60, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(event_type="Console Login" AND mfa_used="Yes", risk_score+40, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(match(eventName,
    "CreateUser|DeleteUser|AttachUserPolicy|CreateAccessKey"),       risk_score+30, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(match(eventName,
    "DeleteBucket|PutBucketPolicy|PutBucketAcl"),                   risk_score+25, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(event_type="API Call",                         risk_score+10, risk_score)

| where risk_score > 0

| stats
    count                   AS event_count,
    values(eventName)       AS api_actions,
    values(sourceIPAddress) AS source_ips,
    values(awsRegion)       AS regions,
    values(mfa_used)        AS mfa_status,
    values(event_type)      AS event_types,
    min(_time)              AS first_seen,
    max(_time)              AS last_seen
    by userIdentity.type, risk_score

| eval alert_title="CRITICAL: AWS Root Account Activity Detected"
| table _time, alert_title, event_types, mfa_status, source_ips,
        api_actions, regions, event_count, risk_score, first_seen, last_seen
| sort -risk_score

/*
TUNING PARAMETERS:
- risk_score threshold: Lower scores (>10) catch read-only root API calls; raise
  to >40 if you want only console logins and destructive actions to alert
- mfa_used filter: Remove the MFA scoring if MFA is not yet enforced to reduce noise
- Whitelist examples:
  | where NOT match(eventName, "^GetAccount|^ListAccount|DescribeBillingView")

FALSE POSITIVES:
- Quarterly billing reviews performed by the finance team via root login
- Break-glass emergency access during a major outage (should have a change ticket)
- Initial AWS account setup activities in newly provisioned accounts
- Automated billing or cost-management tools that use root-level APIs

RECOMMENDED RESPONSE:
1. Confirm whether a change management ticket exists for this root activity
2. Identify the source IP and determine if it belongs to corporate infrastructure
3. Review all API actions taken during the root session in CloudTrail
4. If unauthorized: immediately rotate root credentials and revoke active sessions
5. Enable or verify hardware MFA is enforced on the root account
6. Document findings, close the incident, and trigger a root-cause review

INVESTIGATION QUERIES:
- All root activity in last 24h: index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
  userIdentity.type="Root" earliest=-24h | table _time, eventName, sourceIPAddress, awsRegion
- IAM changes during session: index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
  userIdentity.type="Root" eventSource="iam.amazonaws.com" | table _time, eventName, requestParameters
- S3 changes during session: index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
  userIdentity.type="Root" eventSource="s3.amazonaws.com" | table _time, eventName, requestParameters

DATA SOURCES REQUIRED:
- AWS CloudTrail (management events) — must be enabled in all active regions

PREVENTION MEASURES:
- Enforce hardware MFA token on root account (cannot be delegated)
- Lock root credentials in a physical or enterprise vault (CyberArk, 1Password)
- Enable AWS Config rule: root-account-mfa-enabled
- Set AWS Organizations SCP alert on root usage across all member accounts

RELATED TECHNIQUES:
- T1078 - Valid Accounts (parent technique)
- T1548 - Abuse Elevation Control Mechanism
- T1098.001 - Account Manipulation: Additional Cloud Credentials

CHANGELOG:
v1.0 (2026-02-17): Initial release
*/
